# Lock files
.~lock.*
ROADMAP.md
MEMORY_AUDIT_*.md

# Dev-server stdout/stderr capture (per-app .uvicorn-*.log / .vite-*.log).
# Useful for ad-hoc inspection of a backgrounded server; never committed.
**/.uvicorn-*.log
**/.vite-*.log

# Lineup-pipeline run ledgers: localize-workflow task output, recut/poster/R2
# logs. Provenance for one batch, superseded by the spans pack that batch
# produces (which IS committed). Disposable — regenerate by re-running.
apps/*/backend/scripts/_runs/

# Same idea for a batch's <agent>-spans/_raw/ working dir: the raw workflow
# .output (~1MB each), the placements extracted from it, and the pack snapshot
# exported for the additive diff. All are superseded by the spans pack. The
# BUILDERS in that dir stay tracked — they carry the per-map zone tables, which
# are expensive to rebuild and were nearly lost to `git clean -fd` once already.
apps/*/backend/scripts/*-spans/_raw/*.output
apps/*/backend/scripts/*-spans/_raw/*_passed.json
apps/*/backend/scripts/*-spans/_raw/exported.json
apps/*/backend/scripts/*-spans/_raw/*_args*.json
# Raw localize/gate output. Large (100k+ lines of localizer prose) and derived —
# the tracked <map>.json pack is the artifact. Keep a copy OUTSIDE the repo if you
# may need to rebuild a pack after a zone-table fix; regenerating it means re-running
# the whole localize workflow.
apps/*/backend/scripts/*-spans/_raw/*_localize_raw.json
